# StageConnect: Revolutionizing Audio Connectivity with Open Source Innovation

In the ever-evolving landscape of audio technology, the recent emergence of the **StageConnect** project is making waves for both professionals and enthusiasts alike. By harnessing the power of Analog Devices' A²B technology, StageConnect promises to redefine how we think about audio transmission, merging ease of use with high-quality performance—all while being open source.

## What is StageConnect?

At its core, StageConnect is an Arduino library designed to facilitate the creation of a StageConnect device, which can operate as both a subordinate node and a controlling main device. By utilizing Analog Devices' AD242x-series integrated circuits, this innovative project connects devices like the Behringer WING mixer to the Midas DP48, allowing for the transmission of **32 channels of uncompressed audio** through a single XLR cable. This approach not only simplifies connectivity but also enhances audio quality, transmitting at a stellar **48kHz sampling rate and 32-bit depth**.

### Technical Specifications

The StageConnect system operates via a virtual I2C connection, routed through the A²B link to the Arduino microcontroller. While the recommended cable length for optimal performance is **up to 15 meters**, users have reported success with longer runs, thanks to Behringer's assurances about cable versatility.

Developers can easily implement StageConnect in their projects by including the main library and I2C wrapper class. The setup is straightforward, allowing users to quickly integrate the system into their existing audio setups.

```cpp
#include <StageConnect.h>
#include <ci2c_com.h>

Ci2c_com i2c_com;
StageConnect stageConnect(false, 1, 0xD0, &i2c_com);

void I2C_RxHandler(int numBytes) {...}
void I2C_TxHandler(void) {...}

void setup() {
    Wire.begin(0x3D);
    Wire.onReceive(I2C_RxHandler);
    Wire.onRequest(I2C_TxHandler);
}
```

The simplicity of the code reflects the ethos of the StageConnect project: making high-quality audio technology accessible to all.

## The Community's Response

The Hacker News community has responded enthusiastically to the StageConnect announcement, emphasizing its potential to disrupt traditional audio setups. Discussion threads highlight the excitement around the open source nature of the project, with many users appreciating how it allows for innovation without the constraints of proprietary systems.

One commenter noted the significance of Behringer's willingness to release protocols and specifications openly, stating, “You don’t often see manufacturers being so open about transport protocols or the specs being locked behind expensive paywalls.” This transparency is a breath of fresh air in an industry often criticized for its lack of accessibility.

